1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:02,544
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:06,631
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,802
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,971
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,600
Is Uno there?

7
00:00:17,684 --> 00:00:18,518
[Cita] <i>He is inside. Why?</i>

8
00:00:18,601 --> 00:00:20,061
[Karla] <i>I think he's a spy.</i>

9
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:22,147
<i>Maybe he works for Red Regalia.</i>

10
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,064
[Cita] <i>What?!</i>

11
00:00:23,148 --> 00:00:24,399
[Uno] The truth is,

12
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:26,443
I actually work for Colonel Mercado.

13
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:27,694
Why are you here?

14
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:32,949
I need to secure the laptop
that was turned over to Sir Padua.

15
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,367
Where is he?

16
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,577
[Uno] <i>But he's missing in action.</i>

17
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:36,661
[Cita] <i>Is Atoy still alive?!</i>

18
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,038
- Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom.
- Miss… Miss.

19
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:39,205
Don't say that.

20
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:41,124
I really admire Brother Atoy.

21
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:42,459
Do you admire me too?

22
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:43,918
Ouch. Ouch!

23
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:44,878
What's wrong? [chuckles]

24
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:46,504
Is Atoy here?

25
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,757
We're looking for him. We need his help.

26
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,258
[in English] I don't want to be a Regalia.

27
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:52,635
And I'm ashamed to be
the child of your husband!

28
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:54,596
[Gavin on phone] <i>Mom, I love you.</i>

29
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:58,558
But you're also an enabler
of Dad's evil behavior.

30
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:00,810
[Karla] <i>He's Brother Atoy's colleague.</i>

31
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:03,021
<i>This is Gavin, my friend.</i>

32
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:05,273
- Future boyfriend of Karla.
- What?

33
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:06,399
[in English] Manifesting.

34
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:08,651
We're safe here.

35
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:13,114
How can we be safe if Daddy isn't here?

36
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:14,574
Where are you, Atoy?

37
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:15,575
[mysterious voice] Psst.

38
00:01:15,658 --> 00:01:16,659
[gasps]

39
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:18,787
- [mysterious voice] Psst.
- [gasps]

40
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:20,622
Son of a thread.

41
00:01:20,705 --> 00:01:24,000
[music swells]

42
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:26,044
PREVIOUSLY

43
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:27,462
[music fades]

44
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:30,048
<i>You are the son of the thread.</i>

45
00:01:30,131 --> 00:01:31,549
<i>Emerson, listen.</i>

46
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,717
<i>I need your help</i>

47
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:35,386
<i>and the help of your fellow</i>
<i>children of the thread.</i>

48
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:37,972
[pensive music playing]

49
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:38,890
[Emerson] What is this?

50
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:41,976
Why--

51
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,102
Are you haunting me?

52
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:45,855
Why is your mouth moving in the picture?

53
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:48,399
You're speaking,
but only your mouth is moving?

54
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:49,400
[quirky music playing]

55
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:51,194
What is this? Are you haunting me?

56
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:53,530
Like Tonet?

57
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:55,740
[Atoy] <i>No, no!</i>

58
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:59,410
<i>Emerson, I'm not a ghost yet. Be serious!</i>

59
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:02,539
<i>Act. Prove yourself.</i>

60
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:05,125
<i>I need the help</i>
<i>of the children of the thread.</i>

61
00:02:06,126 --> 00:02:07,752
[whimsical music playing]

62
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:09,003
- [mouthing] <i>Emerson!</i>
- [Cita] Emerson!

63
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:11,548
[babbling]

64
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:12,674
[Cita] Emerson!

65
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,009
Emerson!

66
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,637
Emerson, wake up! Wake up…

67
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:18,930
Ame!

68
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:19,889
Emerson, wake up.

69
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:21,891
- [Ame] I'm here, Miss Cita!
- Wake up!

70
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:24,227
Hurry! Emerson!

71
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,020
Emerson!

72
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:27,564
- [babbling]
- [mouthing] I'll handle it, miss.

73
00:02:27,647 --> 00:02:28,565
[Cita] Quick, quick.

74
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:30,567
- [babbling]
- This will wake up Emerson.

75
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,609
[babbling]

76
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:33,903
- [metals clanging]
- [gasping]

77
00:02:33,987 --> 00:02:35,155
What was that?

78
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:36,656
What was that?!

79
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:37,740
[sneaky music playing]

80
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:39,742
What was that, Ame?

81
00:02:39,826 --> 00:02:44,080
That was so loud,
my eardrums almost broke.

82
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,415
[Ame] Sorry.

83
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:47,750
We didn't know how to wake you up.

84
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:50,336
We found you having a nightmare!

85
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:53,590
[Ame] My gosh!

86
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:58,761
[melancholi music playing]

87
00:02:58,845 --> 00:02:59,929
[puffed exhale]

88
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:05,685
I dreamt of Atoy.

89
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:10,148
He said he needs our help…

90
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:12,609
The children of the thread.

91
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:14,319
[both] Help?!

92
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:16,738
[pensive music playing]

93
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:18,448
Let's save him.

94
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:20,199
[Emerson] Where's Uno?

95
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:22,744
He said he was coming here today.

96
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:25,371
[Gavin, in English] Hello. Good morning!

97
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:29,167
[Emerson] Ame.

98
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:31,836
Maybe you need to call Karla

99
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,630
and Brother Kurt.

100
00:03:33,713 --> 00:03:35,131
Tell them we need an emergency meeting.

101
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:36,883
Right now.

102
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,885
Wait. Isn't that too much?

103
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:41,387
Because it was just a dream.

104
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,140
My gut feeling is different.

105
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,559
[Ame] Oh. Oh, okay.

106
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:48,394
I'll fetch Karla.

107
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:54,817
[suspicious music playing]

108
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:05,703
[music fades]

109
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:10,375
[suave theme music playing]

110
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:12,293
[motorcycle revving]

111
00:04:12,377 --> 00:04:14,212
[sewing machine whirring]

112
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:16,756
- [scratches]
- [snipping]

113
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:20,093
[sewing machine clacking]

114
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:22,720
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

115
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,097
[gunshots]

116
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,765
[clicking]

117
00:04:25,848 --> 00:04:27,183
[snipping]

118
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,060
[music swells]

119
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:33,523
[electronic blipping]

120
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:37,277
I'd like to buy the pink shampoo, please.

121
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,654
Oh. Wait, pretty girl.

122
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:43,574
There's only one left.

123
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:45,243
Good thing you bought it
before we ran out.

124
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:48,079
- Shampoo, please! Hey!
- Hey, Janice.

125
00:04:48,162 --> 00:04:49,372
Pay, pay.

126
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:50,290
Uh--

127
00:04:50,832 --> 00:04:54,168
- This woman.
- Sis, sis, I bought that first.

128
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:55,253
What did you say?

129
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:57,088
I bought it first!

130
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:58,423
[vendor] Hey, Janice!
What's wrong with you?

131
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:01,134
That's for the child! She bought it first!

132
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:02,135
What's wrong with you?

133
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:03,344
- Whatever!
- [vendor] Give it here!

134
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:05,388
I have somewhere to go.
I need to take a bath.

135
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:08,182
You're terrible! She's Olga's daughter!

136
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:09,684
You'll be in trouble.

137
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,686
Give her the shampoo, quick!

138
00:05:11,769 --> 00:05:12,687
Give it.

139
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:13,938
[Janice] Really?

140
00:05:15,606 --> 00:05:17,734
Olga's child is dead.

141
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:19,027
- [smirks]
- [vendor] You're annoying.

142
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:22,113
What are you? A ghost?

143
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,366
You're a fake daughter!

144
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,326
[heavy music playing]

145
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:27,243
[smirks]

146
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,703
I'm not fake.

147
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:30,413
Why are you saying I'm fake?

148
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:33,958
- Olga is a scammer.
- [vendor] Janice!

149
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:37,253
So, for sure, you're her fake daughter!

150
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:41,591
[music swells]

151
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:44,510
Don't insult my mom.

152
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:47,722
And my sister died.

153
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:52,101
And I'm definitely not fake.

154
00:05:53,936 --> 00:05:55,605
Not like your lips.

155
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:58,816
- [gasps] Hey!
- [vendor chuckles]

156
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,985
My lips aren't fake, okay.

157
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:03,321
I took after Angelina Jolie.

158
00:06:03,404 --> 00:06:04,530
[chuckles]

159
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,866
And what you're saying is impossible.

160
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:08,326
Don't mess with me!

161
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:09,494
[suspicious music playing]

162
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:11,454
Olga only has one child!

163
00:06:11,537 --> 00:06:14,832
So, I'm sure that scammer Olga

164
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,210
is just using you to get back

165
00:06:17,293 --> 00:06:20,296
into the barangay, to get aid again!

166
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:23,341
Olga is a scammer!

167
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,009
I know her modus.

168
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:26,511
[smirks] Don't mess with me.

169
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:30,681
You know, you're the one who needs aid.

170
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:33,017
Aid of goodness!

171
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:34,685
Because you lack that.

172
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:36,646
[music fades]

173
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:38,898
- Hey! Oh!
- [laughing]

174
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,441
Janice, what are you doing?!

175
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,276
You're fighting with a child!

176
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,529
- [cackles]
- Are you okay, pretty girl?

177
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:46,447
Oh, you got dirty.

178
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:50,785
It's okay if I fall and get dirty.

179
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:58,251
But my mom will still be beautiful,

180
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:04,298
- even without bee stings on her lips,
- [chuckles]

181
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:06,801
unlike you.

182
00:07:06,884 --> 00:07:08,302
[pensive music playing]

183
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,263
- You're really getting…
- [vendor] Hey. Hey, hey, Janice!

184
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:11,514
- Huh?
- You're getting on my nerves!

185
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:12,807
- [Charmi] Hey!
- [squeals]

186
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:13,808
- Come here.
- Ouch, you're hurting me!

187
00:07:13,891 --> 00:07:15,643
- [shrieking]
- Pull my hair instead.

188
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:18,479
Let's see if you won't swap faces!

189
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:25,528
- [clamoring]
- [screaming]

190
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,905
[music fades]

191
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:31,993
I called you all

192
00:07:32,910 --> 00:07:35,079
because Atoy sent me an SOS.

193
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,664
He called you?

194
00:07:36,747 --> 00:07:39,041
No. I dreamt of him.

195
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:43,379
He said he needs the help
of the children of the thread.

196
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,631
[sneaky music playing]

197
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:46,924
Children of what?

198
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:49,510
What? Children of what?

199
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,053
Children of the thread.

200
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:54,849
Our group, inspired by Brother Atoy.

201
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:58,311
Of course, Thread 1,
our boss, Boss Emerson.

202
00:07:58,394 --> 00:08:00,062
Thread 2, me.

203
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:02,857
Thread 3, MIA, Brother Kurt.

204
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:04,567
[Karla] He'll come here later.

205
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,945
Our mini thread, our muse.

206
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:09,489
[Audrey] Oh!

207
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:11,199
I'm part of that too, right?

208
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:12,325
Yes.

209
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,661
You're the…

210
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,122
adopted thread.

211
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:20,291
- [Karla, in Engilsh] Legit.
- [Uno] Ah!

212
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:22,960
So, does that mean

213
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:26,297
I'm included, because you called me?
Right?

214
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,134
Hmm. Maybe.

215
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,594
[music fades]

216
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:34,597
You can be…

217
00:08:35,473 --> 00:08:38,726
Tape Measure, Pin Tape Measure.

218
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:39,685
[sneaky music playing]

219
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:42,104
Who-- Who…

220
00:08:42,813 --> 00:08:43,773
What's that?

221
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:45,358
I don't understand. What?

222
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:48,611
Tape measure. Tape measure.

223
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:52,865
For measurement. [in English] Measurement.

224
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,743
Because we still need to measure you.

225
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:58,955
You're not really part
of the children of the thread yet.

226
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:01,165
We don't know your skill set,

227
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:04,001
your capacities, your capabilities.

228
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,838
Honestly, you haven't contributed yet,

229
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:09,757
compared to all of us.

230
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:13,261
[music swells]

231
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:19,016
[in English] Going back to the discussion.

232
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,810
[music fades]

233
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:24,814
A special personal mission must be done
by the children of the thread.

234
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:28,150
We'll call this

235
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:32,822
[in English] "Operation Atoy…

236
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:34,323
[suspicious music playing]

237
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:35,533
…Where are you?"

238
00:09:36,701 --> 00:09:38,327
Do you have intel

239
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,330
on Agent Padua's location?

240
00:09:42,248 --> 00:09:48,296
Because, honestly, we don't
have any information about him.

241
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,630
What about you?

242
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:53,009
Do you have any info
on Brother Atoy's last mission?

243
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,343
[in English] Yes.

244
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:57,263
[in English] To retrieve
the high-state decoder.

245
00:09:57,805 --> 00:10:00,933
But he was attacked
by an unidentified syndicate group

246
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:05,354
possibly connected to the Zahran Embassy.

247
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:11,569
Wait. Was this the mission where they
pretended to be the Sokolov brothers?

248
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:14,614
The question is…

249
00:10:16,824 --> 00:10:18,326
Who among them

250
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:21,996
is holding Agent Padua?

251
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,417
That's what we're trying to find out.

252
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,669
Could it be the ambassador?

253
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,921
[music fades]

254
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,966
It's possible, but…

255
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:36,344
Maybe not.

256
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,597
Because as far as I know,

257
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:43,684
our current intel says
he's not in the country.

258
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,603
[suspicious music playing]

259
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:47,396
[Samir, in English]
Nice to meet you, Sir Dmitri.

260
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,231
[in English] This is Samir.

261
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:51,984
[in English] He is the one
I've been telling you about.

262
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,152
[Audrey, in English] Help! Help!

263
00:10:53,235 --> 00:10:54,779
- [in English] Ambassador! Ambassador!
- [Audrey, in English] Help!

264
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:56,113
[in English] Some guy in a mask

265
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:58,115
jumped over the kitchen counter.

266
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:02,620
[in English] He ran and hit my dad
and the ambassador over the head and…

267
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:04,246
he climbed out the hole in the window.

268
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:07,083
[in English] But you're okay, Ms. Audrey.

269
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,293
[in English] He is a master of disguise.

270
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,504
[Samir, in English] He pretends
to be a window cleaner

271
00:11:11,587 --> 00:11:14,090
to sneak into the embassy.

272
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,509
[in English] Do you know this man?

273
00:11:16,592 --> 00:11:20,471
The ambassador's bodyguard.

274
00:11:20,554 --> 00:11:22,098
His name is Samir.

275
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:23,766
S… Samir?

276
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:26,727
I have a strong feeling

277
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:29,397
he's the reason Atoy is missing.

278
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:33,734
[tense music playing]

279
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,873
[in English] Can you please
give him some food? He--

280
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:48,999
[in English] He hasn't eaten
for days. If--

281
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,251
[in English] If he-- If he dies,

282
00:11:50,334 --> 00:11:52,420
you will never know where the laptop is.

283
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:54,088
- [in English] No.
- [in English] You don't understand.

284
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:56,632
[in English] If he dies, you will not know
where the laptop is.

285
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:57,925
[in English] I said, no!

286
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:03,222
[ominous music playing]

287
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:12,940
[speaks in Russian] Delicious!

288
00:12:13,691 --> 00:12:16,694
[in English] That means "delicious".

289
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:20,739
[in English] You see, I learned
your language, Tagalog.

290
00:12:21,323 --> 00:12:22,158
[in English] Good, right?

291
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:23,742
[inhales]

292
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:25,619
Hmm? Smell.

293
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,330
[in English] Oh, look.

294
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:33,586
[in English] Wow, wow.

295
00:12:34,336 --> 00:12:36,881
[in English] Sir. I am--

296
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:38,215
[in English] I am very, very hungry.

297
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:41,844
[in English] Can you… Can you give me
some of that, please, sir?

298
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:45,222
- [in English] Please. Sir. Sir, please.
- [in English] What did you say?

299
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:46,390
- [in English] Give me some, please.
- [Samir, in English] Sir. I like it

300
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,766
- when you call me "Sir".
- [in English] Please.

301
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,143
- [in English] Yes, please, sir.
- Oh.

302
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:50,394
[in English] Please. Give me.

303
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:52,062
[Samir, in English] You want some?

304
00:12:52,146 --> 00:12:53,814
[speaks in Russian] Do you want it?

305
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:54,899
[coughs]

306
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:55,900
[in English] I'm very, very hungry, sir.

307
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:58,360
- [in English] Please, please. Please, sir.
- [speaks in Russian] Take it.

308
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:01,739
- [in Russian] Take it.
- [in English] Please. Ah! Ah… Please, sir.

309
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:04,241
- [in Russian] Take it. Take it!
- [in English] Ah! Very, very hungry, sir.

310
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:05,117
[Samir shouts]

311
00:13:05,659 --> 00:13:07,620
- [groans]
- [tense music playing]

312
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,539
[speaks in Russian] Filthy dog!

313
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:12,666
[grunts and groans]

314
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:16,295
[tense music playing]

315
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:18,088
[speaks in Russian] Punch him!

316
00:13:18,172 --> 00:13:20,883
[Atoy, in English] No.

317
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,760
[grunting and groaning]

318
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:33,562
- [groaning]
- [music swells]

319
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:40,069
[grunting and groaning]

320
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:41,278
[music fades]

321
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,614
So, what are we waiting for?

322
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:44,573
Let's go to the embassy

323
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,825
to spy on Samir.

324
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:48,619
We can't.

325
00:13:49,161 --> 00:13:51,497
The embassy is closed now.
It's the weekend.

326
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:52,665
Closed?

327
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:56,335
If Samir is in the Philippines,

328
00:13:57,002 --> 00:13:58,379
then where could he be now?

329
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:02,591
[in English] Maybe we can go,
um, exercise, running?

330
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:06,929
[in English] Sometimes I go running
in the Acacia Grove on Saturday.

331
00:14:07,012 --> 00:14:07,972
[in English] You've been there?

332
00:14:08,597 --> 00:14:11,809
He invited me to jog in a park, um…

333
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:14,395
[in English] Acacia Grove.

334
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:18,357
He wanted to date me, get to know me.

335
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,275
[Audrey sighs]

336
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:20,693
[Gavin, in English]
What are you saying, Auntie?

337
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:26,699
[in English] So, what I'm saying is,
I can try to bump into him…

338
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:30,744
To get information from him.

339
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:32,162
[Gavin, in English] That's too risky.

340
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,207
[in English] And besides,
we're hiding from Dad. Especially you.

341
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:36,876
Gavin, I don't care.

342
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,544
I just want to help.

343
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:41,630
[in English] I want to find Atoy
just as much as you guys.

344
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:46,510
Didn't Emerson say we need to act now?

345
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,012
Okay.

346
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:53,100
So where is this jogging park
you're talking about, Mama Mary?

347
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:54,351
Oh, no! Um…

348
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:57,438
Mrs. Cutter. No! I mean, Ms. Audrey.

349
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:59,148
Because that's where it will happen.

350
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:02,902
The mission of the children of the thread.

351
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:05,696
[in English] Special personal mission.

352
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:12,077
[in English] "Operation Atoy,
Where are you?"

353
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:19,126
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

354
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:24,048
[in English] Lester, TJ, keep
a closer watch on this dog.

355
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:25,633
[in English] It's just the two of you.

356
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:27,468
[in English] Don't let him escape.

357
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:29,887
[in English] Let's go.

358
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:36,727
[suspicious music playing]

359
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:41,899
[Lily] Atoy. Atoy, can you hear me?

360
00:15:42,566 --> 00:15:44,735
Atoy, here. Eat this, quickly. [grunts]

361
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,738
[sighs, panting]

362
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,783
[panting] Eat, here.

363
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:52,743
[music fades]

364
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:54,078
‪[sighs]

365
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:55,663
[Lily] Atoy.

366
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:56,956
- [sighs]
- [tense music playing]

367
00:15:57,039 --> 00:15:58,165
Where…

368
00:15:58,248 --> 00:15:59,875
- [in English] Please, Sir. Ah!
- [speaks in Russian] Take it! Take it!

369
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,835
[in English] Ah! Very, very hungry, sir.

370
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:02,753
[Samir shouts]

371
00:16:02,836 --> 00:16:04,129
[groans]

372
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:06,966
[in English] The cufflinks.

373
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:10,094
We'll use this in the first stage
of our escape.

374
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:11,512
We'll escape.

375
00:16:11,595 --> 00:16:15,849
[sighs]

376
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,893
[Atoy] Let's go. [inhales]

377
00:16:24,191 --> 00:16:25,025
‪[gasps]

378
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:31,615
- [clatters]
- [sighs]

379
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:36,954
[sighs]

380
00:16:37,037 --> 00:16:38,580
[grunts]

381
00:16:39,206 --> 00:16:43,919
- [groaning, heavy breathing]
- [gate lock rattling]

382
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:45,629
Atoy, Atoy.

383
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:48,424
Here, here.
Hold this, hold this, hold this.

384
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:49,800
[gasps, winces]

385
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:53,137
[groaning, heavy breathing]

386
00:16:57,766 --> 00:16:59,810
- [squealing]
- [clamoring]

387
00:16:59,893 --> 00:17:01,145
How is this going to--

388
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,312
- [mocking chuckle]
- [sneaky music playing]

389
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:04,189
- What?!
- Damn!

390
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,649
Huh?! Get out of here!

391
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:07,943
It's raining. You'll multiply!

392
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,319
You think just because she's a child,

393
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,904
you'll fight with her?! I'll fight you!

394
00:17:10,988 --> 00:17:13,323
The nerve of this woman!

395
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:16,035
Oh, let's see now if you don't go
back to your doctor,

396
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:18,662
so you can get your lips vulcanized!

397
00:17:18,746 --> 00:17:19,788
- [scoffs]
- [music fades]

398
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:20,831
Are you okay, child?

399
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:22,124
That woman.

400
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:23,792
That Janice!

401
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,169
Are you okay?

402
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:27,796
Oh, child?

403
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,214
Don't be sad.

404
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:31,717
Forget what that frog Janice said.

405
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,386
You're not a fake child.

406
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,638
Mama Olga loves you very much.

407
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:38,807
- You know?
- Mmm?

408
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:40,559
I felt

409
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:44,480
she loves me, because she told me.

410
00:17:44,563 --> 00:17:46,482
- Uh-huh.
- And then she hugged me!

411
00:17:46,565 --> 00:17:47,649
See? I told you,

412
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,985
your Mama Olga really loves you.

413
00:17:50,569 --> 00:17:52,488
- I feel sad.
- Oh?

414
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:56,075
Because they called her a scammer.

415
00:17:56,742 --> 00:17:59,995
But Mama is really kind.

416
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,371
Hmm. Mm-hmm.

417
00:18:02,122 --> 00:18:03,290
I hope

418
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:06,210
I won't be separated from Mama.

419
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:11,006
[Charmi] <i>Do you know Ibyang's real parent?</i>

420
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,425
- It's Atoy.
- [in English] For real?!

421
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:16,595
That's why even if I want
to take care of Ibyang

422
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:19,932
and assume the role of her real mother,

423
00:18:20,015 --> 00:18:22,518
of course, that wouldn't be right.

424
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,937
I still need

425
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,523
to give her back to her true parent.

426
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:29,191
To Atoy.

427
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:30,943
[gentle music playing]

428
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:32,736
Just be happy.

429
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:35,072
Okay? Smile now.

430
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:37,282
Smile now.

431
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:40,619
See? You're so beautiful when you smile.

432
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:43,789
And child, don't mention this
to your Mama Olga, okay?

433
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:47,126
Because you know,
she'll pull out all the teeth

434
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:48,627
of that bully Janice.

435
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,462
That bully will get uglier.

436
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:51,630
Just ignore her.

437
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:53,132
[pleasant music playing]

438
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,092
I thought

439
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:58,178
only kids like me bully others.

440
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:00,931
But there are adults who do it too.

441
00:19:01,598 --> 00:19:05,310
And her name even sounds like…

442
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:08,313
Janine!

443
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:10,983
[tense music playing]

444
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:16,405
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

445
00:19:16,488 --> 00:19:19,116
Tape Measure, this is Thread 1.

446
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:21,451
I still don't have a sighting
of Tailor AFAM.

447
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,831
How are your sightings over there?

448
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:26,832
[in English] Over.

449
00:19:27,416 --> 00:19:28,584
Thread 1,

450
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:33,005
I just want to tell you
that the code name you gave me,

451
00:19:33,088 --> 00:19:35,090
I really don't like it.

452
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:36,925
Tape Measure?

453
00:19:37,593 --> 00:19:40,053
It's old. Don't you have another?

454
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:41,555
Well, what else?

455
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:43,849
There aren't many other options.

456
00:19:43,932 --> 00:19:48,020
What do you want? Safety pin? Or…

457
00:19:48,103 --> 00:19:49,021
What else is possible?

458
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:53,233
Safety pin or button. Choose one.

459
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:54,943
What's your status there?

460
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:56,445
Nothing.

461
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:58,030
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

462
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:59,698
Samir isn't here.

463
00:19:59,781 --> 00:20:04,119
I mean, no visuals of Tailor AFAM.

464
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:10,459
I'm thinking, if he doesn't show up here,

465
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:12,836
we're just wasting time.

466
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:16,089
Mama Mary, Adopted Thread.

467
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,425
[in English] Are you guys ready?

468
00:20:18,508 --> 00:20:21,220
Reminder, Thread 1.

469
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:25,849
Mama Mary and Adopted Thread
don't have earpieces. Over.

470
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:29,144
Oh, right. Right.

471
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:30,145
[in English] Sorry.

472
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:33,315
[suspicious music playing]

473
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:34,483
[music fades]

474
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:39,279
Where could Olga be?

475
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,782
We're dead if Boss Red finds out--

476
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:42,741
Psst!

477
00:20:42,824 --> 00:20:43,659
Hide that!

478
00:20:44,576 --> 00:20:46,119
- [thug] Sorry, boss.
- Someone might see that here!

479
00:20:46,203 --> 00:20:47,788
Hide it! Hide it!

480
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:49,748
- [in English] Sorry, boss. Sorry, boss.
- Hide it!

481
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:53,502
[mysterious music playing]

482
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:54,503
[sharp inhale]

483
00:20:59,549 --> 00:21:01,760
[line ringing]

484
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:06,890
Boss, we can't spot Olga.

485
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:11,186
Some people say she jogs here often, but…

486
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:13,689
Not even a shadow.

487
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:15,649
We also went to her house.

488
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:17,150
They said she already moved.

489
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:18,485
She's been gone a while.

490
00:21:18,568 --> 00:21:20,529
Keeps moving around.

491
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:23,657
[in English] Yes, boss.

492
00:21:24,574 --> 00:21:25,993
[in English] Yes, boss. Yes.

493
00:21:26,076 --> 00:21:27,160
We'll keep searching, boss.

494
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:28,495
[in English] Yes, boss.

495
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,498
- [phone blips]
- [in English] Boss.

496
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:33,208
What do we do now?

497
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,335
Where do we find Olga?

498
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:36,628
I don't know!

499
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:41,091
That woman and that mouse Ibyang
are harder to find.

500
00:21:41,633 --> 00:21:44,678
I'm sure they're hiding in Tabang Lupa.

501
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:47,347
They will be easier to catch there.

502
00:21:47,431 --> 00:21:50,976
Boss, let's eat first. I'm hungry.

503
00:21:51,059 --> 00:21:52,352
There!

504
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:55,439
That's what you're good at!
Feeding that snake in your stomach!

505
00:21:56,273 --> 00:21:57,357
Let's go, let's go.

506
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:58,525
[rousing music playing]

507
00:21:58,608 --> 00:22:00,444
[in English] Mama Mary is locked on.

508
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:02,696
[in English] Yes.

509
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:04,281
[Uno] Hmm.

510
00:22:04,364 --> 00:22:07,617
[suspicious music playing]

511
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:08,785
[in English] Yes.

512
00:22:10,704 --> 00:22:11,997
[Gavin] Hey, Tape Measure, behave.

513
00:22:12,581 --> 00:22:14,624
She's Master Cutter's ex,
so you can't flirt with her.

514
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:15,751
Unless you want trouble.

515
00:22:16,335 --> 00:22:18,795
Relax, Adopted Thread.

516
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:19,963
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

517
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:21,006
[sharp exhale]

518
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:22,591
She's not my type.

519
00:22:24,259 --> 00:22:25,969
You might be forgetting.

520
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:27,637
[music fades]

521
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:32,517
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

522
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:34,728
Tape Measure, Tape Measure.

523
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:38,106
I have a sighting of Tailor AFAM.

524
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:40,150
[in English] I already have visuals.

525
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,151
[in English] Be alert.

526
00:22:41,234 --> 00:22:47,949
- [huffs]
- [music swells]

527
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:55,665
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

528
00:22:58,752 --> 00:23:00,545
Let me just remind me of your mission.

529
00:23:00,629 --> 00:23:01,838
[in English] Bump into Samir,

530
00:23:01,922 --> 00:23:03,882
flirt, lure him into a date,

531
00:23:03,965 --> 00:23:05,509
and find out where the Master Cutter is.

532
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:06,802
[Gavin, in English] <i>Good luck, Auntie.</i>

533
00:23:06,885 --> 00:23:07,969
Wait, wait, Gavin.

534
00:23:08,678 --> 00:23:10,180
[Audrey] Do you see Emerson?

535
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:12,224
What's he doing?

536
00:23:12,307 --> 00:23:14,559
- [Emerson, in English] Here, over there.
- [in English] Sir, that's Audrey, right?

537
00:23:14,643 --> 00:23:16,019
- Auntie, let's go. Let's go, Auntie!
- Is that him? Huh? Ah?

538
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:19,356
- [in English] Okay. What! No, no!
- [Kurt] <i>That's him!</i>

539
00:23:19,439 --> 00:23:21,900
The… The ambassador's bodyguard. That's…

540
00:23:21,983 --> 00:23:23,735
Samir! That's Samir!

541
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,113
[Samir, in English] Where do you think

542
00:23:26,696 --> 00:23:28,156
you are going?

543
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:29,950
Go to hell!

544
00:23:30,033 --> 00:23:33,537
[grunting and groaning]

545
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:34,496
‪UP NEXT

546
00:23:34,579 --> 00:23:35,539
There, I… [gasps]

547
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:36,456
I removed it.

548
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:38,083
[speaks softly] I removed it.

549
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:40,836
[in English] What are you talking about?

550
00:23:40,919 --> 00:23:43,004
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

551
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:46,174
♪ <i>One cut, and it's over</i> ♪

552
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:47,759
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

553
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:50,637
